{
  "about": "Geometry.turnHandleSide on both phones: the side (below or above) for the turn and move handles of element, its handle ring standing outsetY off its top and bottom and the turn handle offset beyond that, in page units. reachable is the part of the page a finger can reach, as x, y, w, h. The handle point is offset + outsetY + half the height from the centre along the element's own down (below) or up (above), turned with it. The side is below, unless the point below is outside reachable and the point above is inside it. A rect contains a point on its top and left edges, not its bottom and right ones.",
